+ * which reads ADDR_CRC (0x20000078) and calls the low two bits (CRC_MASK 0x03)
+ * an error when either is set, and then resets the part and looks in the FIFO
+ * for the error events that name the area: 0x20/0x21 for the config,
+ * 0xa0/0xa1/0xa5/0xa6 for the CX. If a config error is found it reflashes; if
+ * the CX is bad it reloads the panel init data. None of that happens here, so
+ * a run cannot currently tell a bad configuration from a bad driver.
